<title>UK: UK regulator demands tighter metals market rules.</title>
<headline>UK regulator demands tighter metals market rules.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's top financial markets regulator, the Securities and Investments Board (SIB), said in a report on Thursday the London Metal Exchange (LME) should reorganise its board, strengthen its executive and provide more market information in the wake of the Sumitomo scandal.</p>
<p>But after a six-month review the SIB rejected calls for sweeping changes, and said the 120-year-old exchange could continue many of its practices such as non-cash clearing. Historic price carries should be used only with appropriate controls, it added.</p>
</text>
